            # Django-pair generation specification                              
                                                                                
            > **PROVENANCE WARNING.** Unlike the Flask specification, this text 
            does not                                                            
            > appear anywhere in the manuscript or in any earlier version of the
            > replication package. The manuscript only *describes* it:          
            "rephrased to                                                       
            > Django's request and response model", covering five behavioural   
            areas (URL                                                          
            > resolution, request object behaviour, view dispatch, response     
            handling,                                                           
            > class-based view behaviour), with templating, application context 
            and                                                                 
            > Blueprints excluded as having no counterpart in the Django URL    
            module.                                                             
            >                                                                   
            > What follows is a reconstruction from that description, written to
            match the                                                           
            > Flask specification's structure, level of detail, and deliberate  
            silences                                                            
            > (it fixes behaviour and the WSGI interface, and names no API      
            symbols beyond                                                      
            > those the behaviour requires). **It is not the original.** If the 
            original                                                            
            > text still exists, replace this file with it before generating,   
            because the                                                         
            > Django oracle's scope is derived from these five areas.           
                                                                                
            ---                                                                 
                                                                                
            Build a WSGI-compatible URL routing and view dispatching layer in   
            Python 3.11.                                                        
            The implementation must support: (1) URL resolution from a declared 
            list of                                                             
            patterns, including literal paths, variable segments with typed     
            converters for                                                      
            integers, strings, slugs, UUIDs and whole paths, and                
            regular-expression                                                  
            patterns with named groups; (2) request object encapsulating method,
            path,                                                               
            headers, query string, and body, with any segments captured from the
            URL                                                                 
            passed to the view; (3) view dispatch, in which the first matching  
            pattern's                                                           
            view is called with the request and the captured segments, and a    
            request                                                             
            matching no pattern yields a 404; (4) response handling, with a     
            response                                                            
            object carrying status code, headers, and body; (5) class-based     
            views, in                                                           
            which a view class dispatches a request to a method named for the   
            HTTP verb,                                                          
            returns 405 with an `Allow` header for a verb it does not implement,
            and                                                                 
            serves HEAD from the GET implementation. The implementation must    
            pass a WSGI                                                         
            compliance check. Provide a complete `pyproject.toml` and a         
            `README.md`.                                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
