            +# Django Framework Implementation Summary                          
            +                                                                   
            +## Overview                                                        
            +                                                                   
            +This implementation provides a complete WSGI-compatible URL routing
            and view dispatching layer inspired by Django, built for Python     
            3.11. The framework meets all requirements specified in the         
            Django-pair generation specification.                               
            +                                                                   
            +## Architecture                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +The framework consists of the following core modules:              
            +                                                                   
            +### 1. `djangoframework/request.py`                                
            +- **HttpRequest class**: Encapsulates HTTP requests with method,   
            path, headers, query string, and body                               
            +- Converts WSGI environ to Django-style META dictionary            
            +- Parses query strings into GET dictionary                         
            +- Handles request body reading from WSGI input                     
            +                                                                   
            +### 2. `djangoframework/response.py`                               
            +- **HttpResponse class**: Carries status code, headers, and body   
            +- **HttpResponseNotFound**: 404 Not Found responses                
            +- **HttpResponseNotAllowed**: 405 Method Not Allowed responses with
            Allow header                                                        
            +- WSGI-compatible response generation                              
            +                                                                   
            +### 3. `djangoframework/converters.py`                             
            +- **Typed URL converters**: int, str, slug, uuid, path             
            +- Automatic conversion of URL segments to appropriate Python types 
            +- Extensible converter system                                      
            +                                                                   
            +### 4. `djangoframework/urls.py`                                   
            +- **URLPattern**: Path-based patterns with typed converters        
            (`<int:id>`, `<str:name>`, etc.)                                    
            +- **RegexURLPattern**: Regular expression patterns with named      
            groups                                                              
            +- **URLResolver**: Matches URLs against pattern lists              
            +- **path()** and **re_path()** helper functions                    
            +                                                                   
            +### 5. `djangoframework/views.py`                                  
            +- **View class**: Base class for class-based views                 
            +- HTTP method dispatch (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)              
            +- Automatic 405 Method Not Allowed responses                       
            +- HEAD request handling via GET methods                            
            +- OPTIONS request support                                          
            +                                                                   
            +### 6. `djangoframework/wsgi.py`                                   
            +- **WSGIApplication**: WSGI-compatible application callable        
            +- URL resolution and view dispatch                                 
            +- Error handling (404, 500)                                        
            +- WSGI response formatting                                         
            +                                                                   
            +## Features Implemented                                            
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ URL Resolution                                              
            +- **Literal paths**: Exact string matching (`/home/`, `/about/`)   
            +- **Variable segments with typed converters**:                     
            +  - `<int:id>` - Integer values                                    
            +  - `<str:name>` - String values                                   
            +  - `<slug:title>` - Slug values (letters, numbers, hyphens,       
            underscores)                                                        
            +  - `<uuid:pk>` - UUID values                                      
            +  - `<path:filepath>` - Path values (including slashes)            
            +- **Regular expression patterns**: Full regex support with named   
            groups                                                              
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Request Object                                              
            +- Encapsulates HTTP method, path, headers, query string, and body  
            +- URL segments captured from patterns passed to views              
            +- Django-style META dictionary for headers and environment         
            variables                                                           
            +- Query string parsing into GET dictionary                         
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ View Dispatch                                               
            +- Function-based views receive request and captured URL segments   
            +- First matching pattern's view is called                          
            +- Unmatched requests return 404 Not Found                          
            +- Exception handling with 500 Internal Server Error                
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Response Handling                                           
            +- Response objects carry status code, headers, and body            
            +- Custom header support                                            
            +- WSGI-compatible response generation                              
            +- Built-in support for common HTTP status codes                    
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Class-Based Views                                           
            +- Views dispatch requests to methods named for HTTP verbs (get,    
            post, put, delete, etc.)                                            
            +- Automatic 405 Method Not Allowed with proper Allow header        
            +- HEAD requests automatically served from GET implementations      
            +- OPTIONS requests return allowed methods                          
            +- View inheritance and customization support                       
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ WSGI Compliance                                             
            +- Full WSGI 1.0 compatibility (PEP 3333)                           
            +- Works with any WSGI server (Gunicorn, uWSGI, mod_wsgi, etc.)     
            +- Proper environ handling                                          
            +- Correct start_response usage                                     
            +- Iterable response format                                         
            +                                                                   
            +## Files Created                                                   
            +                                                                   
            +### Core Framework                                                 
            +- `djangoframework/__init__.py` - Package exports                  
            +- `djangoframework/request.py` - HTTP request handling             
            +- `djangoframework/response.py` - HTTP response handling           
            +- `djangoframework/converters.py` - URL type converters            
            +- `djangoframework/urls.py` - URL pattern matching and resolution  
            +- `djangoframework/views.py` - Class-based views                   
            +- `djangoframework/wsgi.py` - WSGI application                     
            +                                                                   
            +### Configuration                                                  
            +- `pyproject.toml` - Complete project configuration with build     
            system, dependencies, and metadata                                  
            +- `README.md` - Comprehensive documentation with examples and usage
            guide                                                               
            +                                                                   
            +### Testing and Examples                                           
            +- `test_framework.py` - Comprehensive test suite covering all      
            functionality                                                       
            +- `wsgi_compliance_test.py` - WSGI compliance verification         
            +- `specification_verification.py` - Complete specification         
            requirement verification                                            
            +- `example_app.py` - Full-featured example application             
            demonstrating all features                                          
            +                                                                   
            +## Usage Examples                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +### Basic Function-Based Views                                     
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import WSGIApplication, HttpResponse, path    
            +                                                                   
            +def hello_view(request, name):                                     
            +    return HttpResponse(f"Hello, {name}!")                         
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('/hello/<str:name>/', hello_view),                        
            +]                                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +application = WSGIApplication(urlpatterns)                         
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Class-Based Views                                              
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import View, HttpResponse                     
            +                                                                   
            +class ArticleView(View):                                           
            +    def get(self, request, article_id):                            
            +        return HttpResponse(f"Article {article_id}")               
            +                                                                   
            +    def post(self, request, article_id):                           
            +        return HttpResponse(f"Updated article {article_id}")       
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('/articles/<int:article_id>/', ArticleView.as_view()),    
            +]                                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Regular Expression Patterns                                    
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import re_path                                
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    re_path(r'^/archive/(?P<year>[0-9]{4})/$', archive_view),      
            +]                                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Testing Results                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +All tests pass successfully:                                       
            +- ✅ Literal path matching                                         
            +- ✅ Typed converter functionality (int, str, slug, uuid, path)    
            +- ✅ Regular expression pattern matching                           
            +- ✅ Request object functionality                                  
            +- ✅ 404 handling for unmatched patterns                           
            +- ✅ Class-based view method dispatch                              
            +- ✅ 405 Method Not Allowed responses                              
            +- ✅ HEAD request handling                                         
            +- ✅ OPTIONS request support                                       
            +- ✅ WSGI compliance verification                                  
            +                                                                   
            +## Deployment                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +The framework can be deployed with any WSGI server:                
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +# Development                                                      
            +python example_app.py                                              
            +                                                                   
            +# Production with Gunicorn                                         
            +gunicorn example_app:application                                   
            +                                                                   
            +# Production with uWSGI                                            
            +uwsgi --http :8000 --wsgi-file example_app.py --callable           
            application                                                         
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Conclusion                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +This implementation successfully provides a complete Django-style  
            WSGI framework that meets all specification requirements. It        
            demonstrates proper URL routing, request/response handling,         
            class-based views, and WSGI compliance while maintaining clean,     
            readable code architecture.                                         
            diff --git a/README.md b/README.md                                  
            new file mode 100644                                                
            index 0000000..d064076                                              
            --- /dev/null                                                       
            +++ b/README.md                                                     
            @@ -0,0 +1,211 @@                                                   
            +# Django Framework                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +A WSGI-compatible URL routing and view dispatching layer inspired  
            by Django, built for Python 3.11.                                   
            +                                                                   
            +## Features                                                        
            +                                                                   
            +This framework implements the core Django URL routing and view     
            dispatching functionality:                                          
            +                                                                   
            +### 1. URL Resolution                                              
            +- **Literal paths**: Exact string matching                         
            +- **Variable segments with typed converters**:                     
            +  - `int`: Integer values (`<int:id>`)                             
            +  - `str`: String values (`<str:name>` or `<name>`)                
            +  - `slug`: Slug values (`<slug:title>`)                           
            +  - `uuid`: UUID values (`<uuid:pk>`)                              
            +  - `path`: Path values including slashes (`<path:filepath>`)      
            +- **Regular expression patterns**: Full regex support with named   
            groups                                                              
            +                                                                   
            +### 2. Request Object                                              
            +- Encapsulates HTTP method, path, headers, query string, and body  
            +- URL segments captured from patterns are passed to views          
            +- Django-style META dictionary for headers and environment         
            variables                                                           
            +                                                                   
            +### 3. View Dispatch                                               
            +- Function-based views receive request and captured URL segments   
            +- First matching pattern's view is called                          
            +- Unmatched requests return 404 Not Found                          
            +                                                                   
            +### 4. Response Handling                                           
            +- Response objects carry status code, headers, and body            
            +- Built-in support for common HTTP status codes                    
            +- WSGI-compatible response generation                              
            +                                                                   
            +### 5. Class-Based Views                                           
            +- Views dispatch requests to methods named for HTTP verbs (get,    
            post, etc.)                                                         
            +- Automatic 405 Method Not Allowed with proper Allow header        
            +- HEAD requests automatically served from GET implementations      
            +- OPTIONS requests return allowed methods                          
            +                                                                   
            +## Installation                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +pip install djangoframework                                        
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Quick Start                                                     
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import WSGIApplication, HttpResponse, View,   
            path                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +# Function-based view                                              
            +def hello_world(request):                                          
            +    return HttpResponse("Hello, World!")                           
            +                                                                   
            +def hello_name(request, name):                                     
            +    return HttpResponse(f"Hello, {name}!")                         
            +                                                                   
            +def user_detail(request, user_id):                                 
            +    return HttpResponse(f"User ID: {user_id}")                     
            +                                                                   
            +# Class-based view                                                 
            +class ArticleView(View):                                           
            +    def get(self, request, article_id):                            
            +        return HttpResponse(f"Article {article_id}")               
            +                                                                   
            +    def post(self, request, article_id):                           
            +        return HttpResponse(f"Updated article {article_id}")       
            +                                                                   
            +# URL patterns                                                     
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('', hello_world),                                         
            +    path('hello/<str:name>/', hello_name),                         
            +    path('user/<int:user_id>/', user_detail),                      
            +    path('article/<int:article_id>/', ArticleView.as_view()),      
            +]                                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +# Create WSGI application                                          
            +application = WSGIApplication(urlpatterns)                         
            +                                                                   
            +# Run with any WSGI server                                         
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    from wsgiref.simple_server import make_server                  
            +    server = make_server('localhost', 8000, application)           
            +    print("Server running on http://localhost:8000")               
            +    server.serve_forever()                                         
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## URL Patterns                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +### Path Patterns                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +Use `path()` for simple patterns with typed converters:            
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import path                                   
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('articles/', article_list),                               
            +    path('articles/<int:id>/', article_detail),                    
            +    path('articles/<slug:title>/', article_by_title),              
            +    path('files/<path:filepath>/', serve_file),                    
            +]                                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Regex Patterns                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +Use `re_path()` for complex patterns with regular expressions:     
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import re_path                                
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    re_path(r'^articles/(?P<year>[0-9]{4})/$', articles_by_year),  
            +    re_path(r'^articles/(?P<year>[0-9]{4})/(?P<month>[0-9]{2})/$', 
            articles_by_month),                                                 
            +]                                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Class-Based Views                                               
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import View, HttpResponse,                    
            HttpResponseNotAllowed                                              
            +                                                                   
            +class MyView(View):                                                
            +    def get(self, request, *args, **kwargs):                       
            +        return HttpResponse("GET request")                         
            +                                                                   
            +    def post(self, request, *args, **kwargs):                      
            +        return HttpResponse("POST request")                        
            +                                                                   
            +    def put(self, request, *args, **kwargs):                       
            +        return HttpResponse("PUT request")                         
            +                                                                   
            +# Use in URL patterns                                              
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('my-view/', MyView.as_view()),                            
            +]                                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +Class-based views automatically:                                   
            +- Return 405 Method Not Allowed for unsupported HTTP methods       
            +- Include proper Allow header listing supported methods            
            +- Handle HEAD requests using the GET method if available           
            +- Support OPTIONS requests returning allowed methods               
            +                                                                   
            +## Request Object                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +The request object provides access to:                             
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +def my_view(request):                                              
            +    method = request.method          # HTTP method (GET, POST,     
            etc.)                                                               
            +    path = request.path              # URL path                    
            +    query_params = request.GET       # Query string parameters     
            +    headers = request.META           # Headers and environment     
            +    body = request.body              # Request body as bytes       
            +    full_path = request.get_full_path()  # Path with query string  
            +                                                                   
            +    return HttpResponse("OK")                                      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Response Object                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +Create responses with custom status codes and headers:             
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from djangoframework import HttpResponse                           
            +                                                                   
            +def my_view(request):                                              
            +    response = HttpResponse("Custom response", status=201)         
            +    response['Custom-Header'] = 'value'                            
            +    response['Content-Type'] = 'text/plain'                        
            +    return response                                                
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## WSGI Compliance                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +This framework is fully WSGI-compatible and can be deployed with   
            any WSGI server:                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +- **Development**: `wsgiref.simple_server`                         
            +- **Production**: Gunicorn, uWSGI, mod_wsgi, etc.                  
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +# For Gunicorn                                                     
            +# gunicorn myapp:application                                       
            +                                                                   
            +from djangoframework import WSGIApplication, path                  
            +from myviews import my_view                                        
            +                                                                   
            +urlpatterns = [                                                    
            +    path('', my_view),                                             
            +]                                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +application = WSGIApplication(urlpatterns)                         
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Testing                                                         
            +                                                                   
            +The framework includes comprehensive tests covering all            
            functionality:                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +pytest tests/                                                      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Requirements                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +- Python 3.11+                                                     
            +- No external dependencies for core functionality                  
            +                                                                   
